<http://data.silknow.org/object/70d03a78-354a-3649-a85b-593d19dafdb3/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Tapestry hanging in wool and silk. The tapestry is hung behind a large bed, and so only a small area can be seen at the left and right sides. [it has probably been hung in this location since the 18th century, so there is no record of the whole tapestry having been seen]. The left side appears to show the preparation for sacrifice of a bull and the right a cloaked figure, in a woodland scene. The border design has satyrs and medallion busts of Bacchus and Ariadne, among swags of fruit."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/70d03a78-354a-3649-a85b-593d19dafdb3> .

