        ecrm:P3_has_note               "It cannot at present be proved that this set of tapestries hung at Houghton Hall in the time of Sir Robert Walpole, but it is very likely. Walpole, in describing the Embroidered Bedchamber where the set now is, stated \"the hangings are tapestry\"."@en .

